#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# signed_region_distance

#% text
# `signed_region_distance(reg, p)` is the distance from `p` to the boundary of the region, negative inside a solid region.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
signed_region_distance(disk(), [1/2, 0])
#% output
#= -1/2

#% cell
signed_region_distance(rectangle([0, 0], [2, 2]), [1/2, 1])
#% output
#= -1/2

#% text
# Outside it is the distance:

#% cell
signed_region_distance(triangle(), [1, 1])
#% output
#= (1/2)*2^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `region_distance`
